SUMMARY:Transfiguration feast & re-enactment of the 1824 Battle of Samos\, Pythagoreio
LOCATION:Pythagoreio\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Samos's biggest date: the Transfiguration is also the anniversary of the 1824 naval victory over the Ottomans off Mycale. On the evening of 5 August the icon is carried from the church of the Metamorfosi to the harbour (around 21:00)\, followed at 22:00 by a re-enactment of the sea battle with fireworks and a harbour-front glendi\; on 6 August there is a hierarchical liturgy\, wreath-laying at the Lykourgos Logothetis monument and dance groups in the square. Roads into Pythagoreio close from 17:00 on the 5th\, so park outside town and walk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#pythagoreio-transfiguration-feast-re-enactment-of-the-1824-b
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#pythagoreio-transfiguration-feast-re-enactment-of-the-1824-b
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
